+---
+title: 'packet-plumber-v2-network-units — honest counters + real units'
+type: 'feature'
+created: '2026-08-23'
+status: 'in-progress'
+---
+
+# packet-plumber-v2-network-units — honest counters + real units
+
+One coherent job (briefing `packet-plumber-v2-network-units`, 2026-08-23):
+fix the NOC utilization bug (queue-occupancy masquerading as utilization) AND
+speak network-engineer natively (user ruling 2026-08-23: Mbps/Kbps/Gbps
+capacity, bytes for packet sizes).
+
+## The bug (ground truth)
+
+`util_pct = (queued × packet_bandwidth) × 100 / cap_units` — the BACKLOG
+snapshot divided by ONE TICK of capacity. One queued packet on a standard
+pipe reads 120/15 = 800% → clamped 100%. Honest utilization = octets
+transmitted per window ÷ (rate × window) — the ifHCOutOctets/ifSpeed pattern.
+
+## The unit model — RESOLUTION OF A BRIEFING CONTRADICTION (load-bearing)
+
+The briefing's unit model names tier rates **narrow 10 Mbps / standard
+100 Mbps / wide 1 Gbps** AND pins **standard 1500 B transit = 8 ticks** AND
+requires **byte-identical golden timing (T1/T2/replay hash-equal)**. These
+three cannot coexist: with a single SIM_TIME_SCALE, the rate ratio is forced
+to match the sim's capacity ratio (10:15:40 u/s → transit 12:8:3), so real
+rates must be proportional to capacity. 10:100:1000 Mbps implies transits
+80:8:0.8 ticks — a 6.7× pace change on narrow and 3× on wide: a gameplay
+rebalance, forbidden by rule 1, and it would move every T1 golden (rule 4 +
+acceptance).
+
+**Ruling (rules > unit-model proposal):** the sim is untouchable; the unit
+model is a derived canon layer. `SIM_TIME_SCALE = 3333` — the game clock runs
+slowed vs the network clock; pinned by the briefing's own constraint
+(standard 1500 B @ 100 Mbps = 8 ticks: S = 100e6 × 8 / (12000 × 20) =
+3333.33 → 3333; ceil(12000×20×3333/1e8) = 8 ✓). The per-tier line rates are
+THEN DERIVED from the game's own transit (rate_i = frame_bits × 20 × S /
+transit_i): **narrow 66.7 Mbps · standard 100 Mbps · wide 266.7 Mbps**
+(display 67 / 100 / 267 Mbps). The briefing's 10/100/1000 nominal labels are
+arithmetically impossible under the hard rules; this is documented as a
+finding in the PR body ("Decisions & rationale").
+
+**Honest utilization** (windowed, physically bounded): the link's transmission
+WORK is served bandwidth-units (the sim's serialization). Octets transmitted =
+served-units × frame_bytes / packet_bandwidth (12.5 B/unit @ 1500 B/120).
+util = served-units-window × 100 / (W × bundle_cap) — never exceeds 100%,
+exactly 100% at saturation, ~16% for a single residential stream on a
+standard link, 0% for a lone queued packet (backlog ≠ utilization).
+
+## Design
+
+1. **core/units.odin (NEW)** — the canon module (pure, integer, testable):
+   - `SIM_TIME_SCALE :: 3333`, `FRAME_BYTES :: 1500` (uniform MTU; per-class
+     sizes = the briefing's FOLLOW-UP extension point — noted in the PR).
+   - `UTIL_WINDOW_TICKS :: 240` (12 s @ 20 Hz = 30 × the standard 8-tick
+     serialization — exact integer math at saturation, smooth for streams).
+   - `transit_ticks(pb, cap)`, `line_rate_bps(pb, cap, hz)`,
+     `line_rate_bytes_per_tick(...)` (= frame_bytes/transit — the honest
+     reference), `util_pct_window(served, w, pb, cap)`, `format_rate(bps)`
+     (Kbps/Mbps/Gbps auto-scale), `format_bytes(n)` (B/KiB/MiB).
+2. **core/bundles.odin** — per-bundle tx window ring (DERIVED state, never
+   serialized → T1-invisible; replay-rebuildable → stats-check safe):
+   `tx_slot_tick: [dynamic]u64` + `tx_served: [dynamic]u32`, flat W slots per
+   bundle, tick-keyed (pause-safe), zeroed on rebuild (slots renumber),
+   recorded from flow_step's serve totals.
+3. **core/flow.odin** — record each bundle's served-units per tick (the
+   existing serve loop totals, one call per bundle per tick).
+4. **core/stats.odin** — Stats_Pipe_Row gains `tx_octets: u64` (window octets
+   = served × FRAME_BYTES / pb); `util_pct` = the honest windowed formula.
+   CSV: append the tx_octets column (header comment updated). offered/carried/
+   dropped/q stay (backlog + drops views; tests pin them).
+5. **Sim warnings unchanged** (hard rule 1): pipe congestion is already an
+   honest QUEUE signal (fullest lane vs E9 bound — "congestion climbing
+   toward saturation"); queue depth is its own signal by design. The
+   rail/heat-tint amber/red (70/90) rides the honest util_pct.
+6. **Displays go native**:
+   - NOC rail: QUEUES rows gain right-aligned `util%  rate`; the queue bars
+     stay packets-vs-bound; "PIPES AT/OVER 100% (RAW)" → "PIPES AT/OVER 90%
+     (HONEST)" (util ≥ 90); select readout → rate/util/tx/q/drops; POOL label
+     "…(512 PKT)"; DROPS already packets.
+   - Heat-tint labels ride the honest util automatically.
+   - Node health card: `util % (load 1.5 KiB / 400 Mbps)` — node throughput
+     converted with the same mapping.
+   - Tray chips: tier id + rate (`narrow 67M` at 13 px within the 96 px chip).
+7. **Tests**: new units_test; stats_test re-pins (honest util + tx_octets +
+   CSV literal); noc_overlay_test untouched where the skeleton is unchanged.
+
+## Hard rules honored
+
+- Sim math isomorphic: NO data/*.json edits (catalog_hash fold → T1), NO
+  flow/warning/topology semantics change. T1/T2/replay hash-equal — verified
+  by `tools/harness.sh run` (all 45+ demos) with ZERO golden movement.
+- E9/E22 bounds unchanged (6/512, packets stay packets). LOG_VERSION stays 6
+  (no serialized bytes change; the tx ring is derived state).
+- Stats-check live==replay stays green (the ring is replay-identical).
+
+## Tasks (order)
+
+1. core/units.odin + units_test.
+2. bundles.odin ring + flow.odin record call + bundles_rebuild zeroing.
+3. stats.odin honest util + tx_octets + CSV + stats_test re-pins (measure).
+4. Display: noc_overlay rail rework + node_health card + tray chips.
+5. `tools/harness.sh run` full — prove zero golden movement; odin test core +
+   app; tools/ci-local.sh --fast (lint + unit).
+6. KYLE verification (vision-read skill): overlay-check captures — a light
+   single-stream demo (util ~16% on a standard link, NOT 100%) + warn.dem
+   saturation (honest ~100%, queue at bound, drops counting).
+7. PR with Decisions & rationale (the unit-model contradiction ruling, the
+   skill waiver, the zero-golden-movement proof).
