+# v2 network units — honest utilization counters + network-native displays
+
+One job, two halves (briefing `packet-plumber-v2-network-units`,
+2026-08-23): fix the utilization bug the NOC exposed (queue-occupancy
+masquerading as utilization) AND speak network-engineer natively (user
+ruling 2026-08-23: "Mbps/Kbps/Gbps capacity, bytes for packet sizes").
+
+## The bug (fixed)
+
+`util_pct` was `min(100, queued × packet_bandwidth × 100 / cap_units)` — the
+**backlog snapshot divided by ONE TICK of capacity**. One queued packet on a
+standard pipe read 120/15 = 800% → clamped 100%: the NOC claimed every link
+with anything queued was saturated.
+
+**Honest utilization** (the ifHCOutOctets/ifSpeed pattern): the link's
+transmitted work over a rolling window ÷ (line rate × window):
+
+```
+util_pct = served-units(last 240 ticks) × 100 / (240 × bundle_cap)
+tx_octets = served-units × FRAME_BYTES / packet_bandwidth   (12.5 B/unit)
+```
+
+Served-units are what the serve budget actually spent (the transmission
+work). The metric is physically bounded at 100% (the serve budget bounds
+the window's work), reads exactly 100% at saturation, ~16% for a single
+residential stream on a standard link, and **0% for a lone queued packet**
+(backlog ≠ utilization — queue depth is its own signal). The tx ring lives
+in `Bundles` as DERIVED state (same status as `lane_caps`/`drop_sites`):
+rebuilt identically on replay, never serialized — T1/replay byte-identical,
+LOG_VERSION untouched.
+
+## The unit model — RESOLUTION OF A BRIEFING CONTRADICTION
+
+The briefing's unit model named tier rates **10 / 100 / 1000 Mbps** AND
+pinned **standard 1500 B transit = 8 ticks** AND required **byte-identical
+golden timing**. These cannot coexist: a single SIM_TIME_SCALE forces real
+rates proportional to the sim's capacity ratios (10:15:40 u/s → transits
+12:8:3), so 10:100:1000 Mbps would imply transits 80:8:0.8 — a 6.7× pace
+change on narrow and 3× on wide: a gameplay rebalance, forbidden by the
+briefing's hard rules (pace unchanged, T1/T2/replay hash-equal).
+
+**Ruling: the rules win; the unit model is a derived canon layer.**
+`SIM_TIME_SCALE = 3333` is pinned by the briefing's own constraint
+(S = 100e6 × 8 / (12000 × 20) = 3333.33; ceil(12000×20×3333/1e8) = 8 ✓).
+The tier rates derive from the game's own serialization delays
+(rate = frame_bits × logic_hz × S / transit): **narrow 66.7 Mbps ·
+standard 100 Mbps · wide 266.7 Mbps** (displayed 67 / 100 / 267 Mbps).
+The 10/100/1000 nominal labels are arithmetically impossible under the
+hard rules — the honest set is the only one where utilization is consistent
+(any other rate makes narrow read >100% whenever busy). Bundle rates pool
+(a 2-member standard bundle = 200 Mbps); era-3 legacy decay shows honestly
+(a decayed standard link reads 44 Mbps — the rate reflects the sim's
+effective capacity).
+
+Uniform 1500 B frame first, per the briefing; per-class sizes (email
+512 B, streaming jumbo) are the documented FOLLOW-UP extension point
+(`served_to_octets` is the one conversion).
+
+## r2 fold (Perkins r1 @48c0e82 → 8a6f3f5)
+
+- **B1 (blocker) — queue-row glyph collision fixed**: the right-aligned util%
+  overlapped the Best-effort lane's queue-count digit (font-metric-proven:
+  4.8–5.0 px). Lane pitch 108→104, bar 70→64 (count ink now
+  [px+351.2, px+359.6]), util anchor reserve 96→82 (px+416 — "100%"'s first
+  glyph at ~px+372.8, 12 px clearance). KYLE re-read: `P0 … 0 16% 100M` —
+  the util block reads as a clean token. Re-captured.
+- **W2 — tx-ring direct tests** (`bundles_test`): window expiry at the W
+  boundary, slot reuse (stale-check overwrite at tick W+1), same-tick
+  duplicate accumulation (the documented N9 class), rebuild reset with a
+  populated ring, served==0 no-write, defensive bounds.
+- **W3 — `noc_pipe_rows` discriminating test**: hand-built pipes at util
+  89/90 with cap 0 (the old carried>=cap predicate is provably dead) + a
+  carried-saturated row at util 0 that must NOT count; amber-boundary pin
+  for `noc_queue_rows` (N4).
+- **Notes**: N1 zero-cap → transit 0 (no rate, no 800 Mbps inversion) with
+  `line_rate_bps(…,0)` pin; N8 `line_rate_bytes_per_tick` removed (dead);
+  N2 stale 96-px comments → 112; N4 section headers + queue-row predicate
+  read the catalog tunables (lane bound, pool cap, amber/red pcts) — no
+  hardcoded 90/6/512; N5 stats stream marker v1→v2 (the P-row schema
+  changed); N6 CSV literal fixture now a self-consistent honest pair
+  (util 16 + tx 7500 = 600 served units); N9 same-tick class documented on
+  the ring; N12 Bundles doc corrected (flow-derived ring, not a pure
+  topology function).
+- **W1 UNCHANGED** (escalated to the user via Gru): the derived
+  67/100/267 Mbps ladder stands as-is in this fold.
+- Verification: 48/48 harness demos green (zero golden movement), core
+  242/242, render 77/77, stats live==replay byte-identical, fast gates
+  1–2 green.
+
+## What changed
+
+| file | change |
+|---|---|
+| `core/units.odin` (new) | the canon: SIM_TIME_SCALE, FRAME_BYTES, UTIL_WINDOW_TICKS (240 = 12 s), transit/rate/octet/util helpers, rate+byte formatters |
+| `core/bundles.odin` | per-bundle tx window ring (derived, non-serialized) + record/window procs |
+| `core/flow.odin` | record each bundle's served-units per tick |
+| `core/stats.odin` | honest windowed util_pct + tx_octets column (CSV appended) |
+| `app/render/noc_overlay.odin` | rail native: QUEUE DEPTH VS E9 BOUND (6 PKT) rows + right-aligned honest util% + rate; PIPES AT/OVER 90% (HONEST); POOL (512 PKT); select readout rate/tx/q/drops |
+| `app/render/node_health.odin` | node card: "150% (load 1.5 KiB / 33 Mbps)" |
+| `app/render/tray.odin` + `app/main.odin` | link chips "standard 100M" (chip 96→112 px) |
+| `app/render/spawn_fx.odin` | shadow_clone deep-copies the tx ring (a missed clone corrupted the live state — caught by the full harness run) |
+| tests | units_test (new); stats_test re-pinned to the honest measured values; noc row-count pins unchanged |
+
+## Golden evidence (the hard rules)
+
+- **Zero golden movement**: `tools/harness.sh run` — **48/48 demos green**
+  (T1 per-tick hashes + T2 software pixels + the replay gate), `git status`
+  clean on `goldens/`. No `data/*.json` bytes changed (catalog_hash fold →
+  T1) and no sim semantics moved; only the stats *stream* (dev tool, not a
+  golden) + unit-test pins changed.
+- **Stats stream replay-identity** (live == replay) green (gate 12).
+- **Full local CI 13/13 gates green** (`tools/ci-local.sh --mac`).
+- Sim warnings untouched: pipe congestion is already an honest QUEUE signal
+  (fullest lane vs E9 bound — "climbing toward saturation"); the rail's
+  amber/red (70/90) rides the honest util_pct.
+
+## KYLE verification (glm-4.6v, acceptance)
+
+Synthetic single-stream demo (one email packet per 2.4 s on one standard
+link, the credit-gated residential cadence), rendered via the PP_DEBUG
+`overlay-check` verb (the shipped rail code, rlsw software renderer):
+
+- **Single stream: util reads 16%** (stats: 600 served units / 240×15 —
+  the exact 16.67% → 16), queue depth 0–1 in the busy lane, **rate "100M"**,
+  drops 0, no pipes over 90% — the old metric read 800%-clamped-100 for the
+  same backlog. KYLE read the rail verbatim: `P0 … 016% 100M`.
+- **Saturation (warn.dem @45s): the saturated pipe reads 100% honest util
+  with its queue AT the 6-packet bound**, E9 drops 202 counted, per-class
+  loss 92% on streaming — queue depth and utilization are now separate,
+  honest signals. A legacy-decayed link reads "44M" — the rate reflects the
+  6.3 decay (cap 7 → 44.4 Mbps), network-native truth.
+- All rail labels native: "QUEUE DEPTH VS E9 BOUND (6 PKT)", "POOL VS E22
+  CAP (512 PKT)", "PIPES AT/OVER 90% (HONEST)".
+
+## Decisions & rationale
+
+- **Physics-consistent rates over the 10/100/1000 nominal ladder** — the
+  hard rules (pace unchanged, hash-equal goldens) are unsatisfiable with the
+  nominal rates; the derived set is the only one where honest utilization is
+  consistent with the game's own congestion model. If the nominal ladder is
+  ever wanted, it requires a transit rebalance + full golden re-bless as its
+  own job.
+- **Served-units as the octet counter** — the sim's transmission work is
+  quantized per bandwidth-unit (12.5 B/unit at 1500 B / 120); counting
+  completions × 1500 overcounts during residual-completion bursts (util
+  could transiently exceed 100). Served-units are bounded, monotone, and
+  exactly 100% at saturation.
+- **Window 240 ticks (12 s)** — 30 × the standard 8-tick serialization:
+  exact integer math at saturation, smooth for light streams. Resets on
+  bundle rebuilds (slot renumbering) — the rail's util dips after topology
+  edits and recovers within 12 s; documented in the code.
+- **bmad-build skill waiver** — bmad-build is unusable on packet-plumber
+  (`_bmad/scripts/` ships no `render_skill.py`; the bmm/gds dual-module
+  config makes the renderer's short-token resolution ambiguous) — waived
+  per Silas ruling 2026-08-21; the briefing was self-contained. This job's
+  plan lives at
+  `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/spec-packet-plumber-v2-network-units.md`.
